[38;2;124;124;124m\beta^{(X,x)}_X(\operatorname{id}_X)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe cocone compatibility condition for $f: (X, x) \to (Y, y)$ in $\int F$ says $[0m[38;2;124;124;124m\beta^{(Y,y)} \circ f_* = \beta^{(X,x)}$. Evaluating at $\operatorname{id}_X$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\beta^{(X,x)}_X(\operatorname{id}_X) = \beta^{(Y,y)}_X(f_* (\operatorname{id}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m_X)) = \beta^{(Y,y)}_X(f) = P(f)(\beta^{(Y,y)}_Y(\operatorname{id}_Y)) = P(f)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(b_{(Y,y)})$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $b_{(X,x)} = P(f)(b_{(Y,y)})$ whenever $f: (X,x) \to (Y,y)$, i.e., whenever [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$f: X \to Y$ with $F(f)(y) = x$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Define $\gamma: F \to P$.** For each $C \in \mathfrak{C}$ and $c \in F(C)$, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe pair $(C, c)$ is an object of $\int F$, so we have $b_{(C,c)} \in P(C)$. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mDefine:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\gamma_C(c) = b_{(C,c)}$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Check $\gamma$ is natural.** For $h: C' \to C$ in $\mathfrak{C}$ and $c \in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mF(C)$, we need $\gamma_{C'}(F(h)(c)) = P(h)(\gamma_C(c))$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNote that $h: C' \to C$ with $F(h)(c) \in F(C')$ gives a morphism $h: (C', F(h)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(c)) \to (C, c)$ in $\int F$ (since $F(h)(c) = F(h)(c)$ ✓). The cocone [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcompatibility gives:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$b_{(C', F(h)(c))} = P(h)(b_{(C, c)})$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThat is, $\gamma_{C'}(F(h)(c)) = P(h)(\gamma_C(c))$. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Check $\gamma \circ \alpha^{(X,x)} = \beta^{(X,x)}$.** At component $C$, for [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$g \in \operatorname{Hom}_{\mathfrak{C}}(C, X)$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$(\gamma \circ \alpha^{(X,x)})_C(g) = \gamma_C(\alpha^{(X,x)}_C(g)) = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\gamma_C(F(g)(x)) = b_{(C, F(g)(x))}$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, $g: C \to X$ with $F(g)(x) \in F(C)$ gives a morphism $g: (C, F(g)(x)) \to [0m[38;2;124;124;124m(X, x)$ in $\int F$. The cocone compatibility gives:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\beta^{(C, F(g)(x))} = \beta^{(X,x)} \circ g_*$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mEvaluating at $\operatorname{id}_C$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$b_{(C, F(g)(x))} = \beta^{(C,F(g)(x))}_C(\operatorname{id}_C) = \beta^{(X,x)}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m_C(g_*(\operatorname{id}_C)) = \beta^{(X,x)}_C(g)$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $(\gamma \circ \alpha^{(X,x)})_C(g) = \beta^{(X,x)}_C(g)$. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Check uniqueness.** Suppose $\gamma': F \to P$ also satisfies $\gamma' \circ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\alpha^{(X,x)} = \beta^{(X,x)}$ for all $(X,x)$. For any $C$ and $c \in F(C)$, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mconsider $(C, c) \in \int F$ and evaluate $\gamma' \circ \alpha^{(C,c)} = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\beta^{(C,c)}$ at $\operatorname{id}_C$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\gamma'_C(\alpha^{(C,c)}_C(\operatorname{id}_C)) = \beta^{(C,c)}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m_C(\operatorname{id}_C) = b_{(C,c)}$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\gamma'_C(F(\operatorname{id}_C)(c)) = \gamma'_C(c) = b_{(C,c)} = \gamma_C(c)$[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $\gamma' = \gamma$. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Conclusion:** $F$ satisfies the universal property of the colimit of $D$. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$$\operatorname{colim} D \cong F$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is the **density theorem** (co-Yoneda lemma): every presheaf $F: [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathfrak{C}^{opp} \to \mathfrak{Set}$ is the colimit of representable [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpresheaves indexed by its category of elements.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$$F \cong \operatorname{colim}_{(X,x) \in \int F} \operatorname{Hom}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m_{\mathfrak{C}}(-, X)$$[0m

